From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Treggat <taggert2222@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:48:36 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 11/27] sycl : command-graph replay cache and fast top-k
 sampling

Runtime switches, all default off:
- GGML_SYCL_ENABLE_GRAPH: record decode graphs once and replay them from a
  keyed cache (exact node/shape/pointer signature, LRU of 64); graphs over
  GGML_SYCL_GRAPH_MAX_TOKENS rows (default 32) stay eager; ops that cannot be
  recorded fall back to eager; GGML_SYCL_GRAPH_STATS / _SELFTEST for checks
- LLAMA_SAMPLER_FAST_TOPK: one-pass top-k when the chain before it is a no-op
- LLAMA_MTP_DEFER_CATCHUP: experimental, lowers MTP acceptance - keep off
Also removes the stale CONCAT graph block and adds host/graph timing
instrumentation (GGML_SYCL_GRAPH_TIME, LLAMA_HOST_PROF).

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
